{# Report a vulnerability: how to report vulnerabilities in VORNAC products
   and services.

   Content and commitments come from the Drive document "Website
   Schwachstelle melden: Texte und Aufgaben" (as of 24 November 2026). The
   wording was set by André on 2026-11-27: the register of the TLPT
   statements, written for information security officers and security
   leads. Do not change commitments or rules without asking; the German
   version is src/de/security.njk.

   well-known/security.txt names this page as a Policy. If the path changes,
   change the file as well.

   `data-no-crosslink` on the text block keeps the automatic glossary links
   out of the policy text. #}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block extraHead %}
{% include "partials/prose-styles.njk" %}
{% set schemaType = "WebPage" %}{% set schemaAboutOrg = true %}
{% include "partials/page-schema.njk" %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<main class="relative z-10 py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 prose" data-no-crosslink>

        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl mb-10 lg:mb-14">Report a vulnerability</h1>

        <p class="text-lg">Report vulnerabilities in VORNAC products and services by email to <a href="mailto:security@vornac.com">security@vornac.com</a>. Coordinated vulnerability disclosure applies: details of a vulnerability are published only once it has been fixed or on a date agreed with VORNAC. VORNAC acknowledges every report within two business days.</p>

        <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">

            <section id="report" class="space-y-4">
                <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl">What a report should contain</h2>
                <p>A report should contain:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
                    <li>the affected product or service, including the version if known</li>
                    <li>a description of the vulnerability and its potential impact</li>
                    <li>the steps to reproduce it, where possible with screenshots or a proof of concept</li>
                    <li>a contact for follow-up questions</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="commitments" class="space-y-4">
                <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl">What VORNAC commits to</h2>
                <ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
                    <li>acknowledgement of receipt within two business days</li>
                    <li>review of every report, with updates on progress</li>
                    <li>a fix for confirmed vulnerabilities as quickly as possible, and notice to affected customers</li>
                    <li>on request, credit as the finder of the vulnerability once it has been fixed</li>
                    <li>no legal action against anyone who reports a vulnerability in good faith and in line with the rules on this page</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="rules" class="space-y-4">
                <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl">Rules for reporters</h2>
                <ul class="list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
                    <li>Do not publish details of the vulnerability before it has been fixed, unless a date has been agreed with VORNAC.</li>
                    <li>Do not access, modify or delete other people's data, and do not disrupt customer systems.</li>
                    <li>Test only as far as necessary to demonstrate the vulnerability.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

        </div>

        <p class="mt-12">The contact address is also published in machine-readable form in <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a> under RFC 9116.</p>

    </div>
</main>
{% endblock %}
